<task id="006" project="spaarke-intake-pipeline-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-03 cleanup PR (part 2): §10.1 item 7 threaded reply via Graph createReply/createReplyAll + item 8 docs (ADR-036:104, sprk_backgroundjobrun note)</title>
    <phase>0 Foundations and cleanup</phase>
    <gate>after 005 (same branch / same PR); the live test send needs owner OK and the shared mailbox</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies BFF .cs on the outbound email send path (tags bff-api); a wrong fallback silently sends unthreaded mail.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Single-component change in EmailChannelSender with a precise contract from spec FR-03(c–e); Graph createReply is a documented API.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P0-A2</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>005</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, backend, unit-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Make a server-side email send that carries `InReplyToMessageId` go out as a real threaded reply: locate the parent message in the sending mailbox and use Graph `createReply` (or `createReplyAll`) on it, then send, so `In-Reply-To` and `References` are set by Exchange. Sends without `InReplyToMessageId` are unchanged; a missing parent fails with a ProblemDetails error code and never silently sends unthreaded. Also fix the stale ADR-036:104 text (item 8 docs).</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in Microsoft Graph mail (messages, createReply, internetMessageHeaders) and the BFF CommunicationService / channel-sender design. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>`EmailChannelSender` has a reply branch (createReply → update draft body/recipients/attachments/server-send marker → send) used when `InReplyToMessageId` is set; unit tests cover reply, non-reply and parent-not-found; `docs/adr/ADR-036-background-job-infrastructure.md` line 104 states run history is process-local today (`InMemoryBackgroundJobStore`) with `sprk_backgroundjobrun` as target state; the data-model note is confirmed or corrected.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-03 item 7 and acceptance (c), (d), (e); item 8 docs. Verification §7: `EmailChannelSender.cs:205-231` builds a new `Message`; the only header is the server-send marker (:229-232); `InReplyToMessageId` is stored (CommunicationService.cs:1208, :3241) and used only for thread joining. Graph rejects custom `internetMessageHeaders` not starting with `x-`, so In-Reply-To cannot be set by header — createReply is the fix. FR-20 (Phase 2 email return) depends on this. Verification §8: `docs/data-model/sprk_backgroundjobrun.md:8` already states "deployed but unused"; `.claude/adr/ADR-036-background-job-infrastructure.md` already says target state, so no `.claude/` edit is needed. This task commits on the task 005 branch: same PR.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Channels/EmailChannelSender.cs (BuildGraphMessage :201-240 and the send call)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationService.cs (only if InReplyToMessageId must be passed through to ChannelSendRequest; check :867, :1209, :3248 first)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/regression/Intake10_1_Item7_EmailChannelSenderThreadedReplyTests.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">docs/adr/ADR-036-background-job-infrastructure.md (:104)</file>
      <file role="modify">docs/data-model/sprk_backgroundjobrun.md (:8, only if still inaccurate)</file>
      <file role="modify">docs/architecture/communication-service-architecture.md (describe the reply branch)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Channels/EmailChannelSender.cs (existing shared-mailbox vs user-mode addressing and outcome mapping :195-200 to mirror)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Errors/ProblemDetailsHelper.cs (stable errorCode)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="005" status="pending">Same PR; both edit CommunicationService.cs (005 at ~:4554).</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-045">Scope: the reply branch. It stays inside `CommunicationService` → `EmailChannelSender` (the server side of the canonical send); no new send path, no direct Graph call from another service.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">Scope: parent-not-found and createReply failures. Return a ProblemDetails with a stable `errorCode` (e.g. `communication.reply_parent_not_found`); never fall back to a new unthreaded message.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: sends without `InReplyToMessageId`. Byte-for-byte the same Graph request as today (regression-tested).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: custom headers on the reply. Only `x-`-prefixed `internetMessageHeaders`; the existing server-send marker must still be present on the sent reply.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">Scope: logs on the reply path. Message ids, mailbox id and outcome only; no subject or body text.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the live test send (acceptance c). Only with the owner's explicit OK, from the dev shared mailbox, to an owner-named test recipient; never to a real external address.</constraint>
    <constraint source="bff-extensions">Scope: the PR (shared with 005). Placement Justification, publish-size delta vs fresh master, ≤ 60 MB, no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
  </constraints>

