    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Channel sender" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Channels/EmailChannelSender.cs">Shared-mailbox addressing, NoTransientRetryOption outcome mapping, server-send marker header.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Determine what `InReplyToMessageId` holds (Graph id vs RFC internetMessageId) from CommunicationService and the inbound processor; design the parent lookup accordingly (Graph `messages?$filter=internetMessageId eq '…'` in the sending mailbox if it is an RFC id).</step>
    <step order="2">Add the reply branch to EmailChannelSender: lookup parent → createReply (createReplyAll when the request asks reply-all) → PATCH draft with body, To/Cc/Bcc, attachments, server-send marker → send; map failures to the existing outcome codes; parent not found → typed failure surfaced as ProblemDetails.</step>
    <step order="3">Pass `InReplyToMessageId` through `ChannelSendRequest` only if it is not already reachable.</step>
    <step order="4">Write EmailChannelSenderReplyTests (mocked Graph): reply uses createReply on the parent; non-reply unchanged; parent missing → error, no send; marker header present on the reply.</step>
    <step order="5">Fix ADR-036 full doc :104 and verify the data-model note; describe the reply branch in communication-service-architecture.md.</step>
    <step order="6">`dotnet build`, `dotnet test`.</step>
    <step order="7">With owner OK: deploy to dev via `/bff-deploy`, send one test reply from the dev shared mailbox, and record In-Reply-To/References headers and Outlook threading (screenshot path) in notes.</step>
    <step order="8">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]`.</step>
    <step order="9">Record deviations in `projects/spaarke-intake-pipeline-r1/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>The live test send and the dev deploy need the owner's explicit OK and a mailbox with Exchange RBAC for Applications (plan R8). If either is missing, STOP at step 7, ship the code-level tests, and mark acceptance (c) pending in notes rather than sending from another mailbox.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the server-send marker cannot be carried on a createReply draft, STOP and escalate — losing it re-files attachments on the inbound path.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>reuse-scan.md row 12 (outbound reply): `EmailChannelSender.cs:22`, CAPABILITY-INDEX row 12; verdict "fix in place". New surface: one private reply branch and one test file.</existing>
    <extension>Yes — extends EmailChannelSender in place; no new service or endpoint.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Replies arrive as new, unthreaded mail (no In-Reply-To/References), so FR-20's threaded email return and FR-03(c) fail.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Channels/EmailChannelSender.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/regression/Intake10_1_Item7_EmailChannelSenderThreadedReplyTests.cs</output>
    <output type="docs">docs/adr/ADR-036-background-job-infrastructure.md</output>
    <output type="docs">docs/architecture/communication-service-architecture.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a send with `InReplyToMessageId` whose parent exists in the sending mailbox, the sender calls createReply on that parent and sends the draft; no new-message `sendMail` call is made.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a send without `InReplyToMessageId`, the Graph request is unchanged from today (FR-03d).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: given a parent that cannot be found, the send fails with a ProblemDetails stable error code and nothing is sent (FR-03e).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The sent reply carries the server-send marker header and no non-`x-` custom header.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">With owner OK, a dev test send shows In-Reply-To and References and threads under the original in Outlook (FR-03c); otherwise recorded as pending with the reason.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ADR-036 full text no longer claims a `sprk_backgroundjobrun` row is persisted per invocation today.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Build and all tests pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Seeding proof requested for the parent-not-found test (a silent unthreaded fallback is the defect this task removes): make the branch fall back to a new message, confirm the test fails, restore.</notes>

